Patch summary:
Store a 4:2:0 YUV ColorBuffer (YV12, YV21, NV12, NV21) as RGBA8 when the
device cannot create its format, converting the guest's YUV bytes on upload
with the GL YUVConverter's BT.601 limited-range matrix. Direct3D 12 has no
three-plane YUV format, so on WSL2 (Mesa's Dozen) the ColorBuffer of a YV12
frame from a software video decoder was not created ("Format
VK_FORMAT_G8_B8_R8_3PLANE_420_UNORM is not supported"), and SurfaceFlinger
aborted on the buffer ("Failed to create a valid texture ... format:842094169"),
restarting Android's framework: a Play Store trailer froze every app window.
The device's support comes from the queried support list, as image creation
uses it: ImageSupport::IsFormatSupported() reports every color format
supported. The format is reported supported to the guest; the compositor and
display sample such a ColorBuffer as RGBA8 (with its YV12 format the
compositor found no pipeline, a fatal error that ended crosvm); the guest's
images bound to it, and its image format queries for them, take RGBA8 too;
and reading it back fails, leaving the guest's own YUV bytes in place.
